  <key id="d0" for="node" attr.name="entity_type" attr.type="string" />
  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;ANET SMITS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Anet Smits is a Dutch association football player known for her contributions to the sport and her dedication to promoting gender equality. She has played for top-tier clubs like Ajax and PSV Eindhoven and has been recognized for her achievements and commitment to inspiring young women in football."&lt;SEP&gt;"Anet Smits is a badminton player whose ranking has improved significantly, catching the attention of fans and enthusiasts."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0311</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NL GENDERGAP MAINTENANCE PROJECT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The NL Gendergap maintenance project is a Dutch Wikipedia initiative aimed at increasing the visibility of women on the online encyclopedia and addressing the significant disparity in representation between men and women."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0311</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DR. SASKIA WOUTERSEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dr. Saskia Woutersen is a lead researcher on the NL Gendergap maintenance project and has praised Anet Smits for her remarkable career and dedication to promoting gender equality in sports."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0311</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MARIANNE VAN LEEUWEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Marianne van Leeuwen is a sports journalist and contributor to the NL Gendergap maintenance project who has highlighted Anet Smits as an inspiration to many young women in the Netherlands and beyond."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0311</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AJAX&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ajax is a top-tier football club where Anet Smits has played and is known for its strong women's football team."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0311</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PSV EINDHOVEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PSV Eindhoven is another top-tier football club where Anet Smits has played and is known for its strong women's football team."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0311</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WIKIPEDIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Wikipedia is an online encyclopedia where the NL Gendergap maintenance project works to improve the representation of women."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0311</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BADMINTON WORLD FEDERATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Badminton World Federation provides official rankings for badminton players, including Anet Smits."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Badminton World Federation tracks rankings and statistics for badminton players globally."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0311</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WIKIPROJECT BADMINTON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"WikiProject Badminton is a project within Wikipedia focused on improving articles related to badminton."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0311</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AMSTERDAM, NETHERLANDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Amsterdam, Netherlands is the city where Anet Smits made her surprise move to badminton and where the WikiProject Badminton focus list is based."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0311</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EUROPEAN BADMINTON CHAMPIONSHIPS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The European Badminton Championships is an international badminton tournament where Anet Smits is set to make her debut."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0311</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DUTCH BADMINTON CHAMPIONSHIPS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Dutch Badminton Championships is a national badminton tournament where Anet Smits performed impressively, earning her a spot on the WikiProject focus list."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0311</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DUTCH FOOTBALLER OF THE YEAR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dutch Footballer of the Year is an award given annually to the best football player in the Netherlands, which Anet Smits won in 2017."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0311</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TOP-TIER CLUBS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Top-tier clubs refer to elite football clubs where Anet Smits has played, such as Ajax and PSV Eindhoven."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0311</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GENDER GAP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gender gap refers to the disparity in representation between men and women, which the NL Gendergap maintenance project aims to address."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0311</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ONLINE REPRESENTATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Online representation refers to the visibility of women on online platforms like Wikipedia, which the NL Gendergap maintenance project seeks to improve."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0311</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WOMEN'S FOOTBALL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Women's football refers to the sport of football played by women, which Anet Smits has been a trailblazer for in the Netherlands."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0311</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPORTS JOURNALISM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sports journalism refers to the field of reporting and writing about sports, which Marianne van Leeuwen practices."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0311</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPORTS COMMUNITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sports community refers to the network of athletes, coaches, and supporters involved in sports, which includes Anet Smits and her former teammates and coaches."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0311</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FORMER TEAMMATES AND COACHES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Former teammates and coaches refer to the people Anet Smits has worked with in her football career, including her former coach Ronald Koeman."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0311</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RONALD KOEMAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ronald Koeman is a former coach of Anet Smits and has expressed admiration for her bold move to badminton."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0311</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WIKIPROJECT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"WikiProject is a collaborative effort where fans and enthusiasts track and discuss the progress of players like Anet Smits."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0311</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHAMPIONSHIPS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
